 *******************************************************************************
 **                                                                           **
 **           Bethe Salpeter equation (BSE) for excitation energies           **
 **          solved with and without Tamm-Dancoff approximation (TDA)         **
 **                                                                           **
 *******************************************************************************
  
 BSE| No cutoff given for occupied orbitals
 BSE| No cutoff given for empty orbitals
 BSE| First occupied index                                                     1
 BSE| Last empty index (not MO index!)                                       230
 BSE| Energy of first occupied index [eV]                               -427.369
 BSE| Energy of last empty index [eV]                                    143.855
 BSE| Energy difference of first occupied index to HOMO [eV]             420.544
 BSE| Energy difference of last empty index to LUMO [eV]                 144.256
 BSE| Number of GW-corrected occupied MOs                                     52
 BSE| Number of GW-corrected empty MOs                                       230
 BSE|
 BSE| No truncation of BSE matrices applied
 BSE|

 *** WARNING in bse_util.F:1622 :: Keyword NUM_PRINT_EXC_DESCR is either ***
 *** negative or too large. Printing exciton descriptors up to           ***
 *** NUM_PRINT_EXC.                                                      ***

 BSE| Total peak memory estimate from BSE [GB]                         1.066E+01
 BSE| Peak memory estimate per MPI rank from BSE [GB]                      0.167
 BSE|
 BSE| Diagonalizing aux. matrix with size of A. This will take around 5.E+00 s.
 BSE| Diagonalizing A. This will take around 5.E+00 s.
 BSE|
 BSE|
 BSE| **************************************************************************
 BSE| *   Bethe Salpeter equation (BSE) with Tamm Dancoff approximation (TDA)  *
 BSE| **************************************************************************
 BSE|
 BSE| The excitations are calculated by diagonalizing the BSE within the TDA:
 BSE|
 BSE|                       A X^n = Ω^n X^n
 BSE|
 BSE| i.e. in index notation:
 BSE|
 BSE| sum_jb ( A_ia,jb   X_jb^n ) = Ω^n X_ia^n
 BSE|
 BSE| prelim Ref.: Eq. (36) with B=0
 BSE| in PRB 92,045209 (2015); http://dx.doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevB.92.045209 .
 BSE|
 BSE|
 BSE| i,j:       occupied molecular orbitals, i.e. state in          [   1,  52]
 BSE| a,b:       unoccupied molecular orbitals, i.e. state in        [  53, 282]
 BSE| n:         Excitation index
 BSE|
 BSE| A_ia,jb = (ε_a-ε_i) δ_ij δ_ab + α * v_ia,jb - W_ij,ab
 BSE|
 BSE| ε_...:                 GW quasiparticle energy
 BSE| δ_...:                 Kronecker delta
 BSE| α:                     spin-dependent factor
 BSE| v_...:                 Electron-hole exchange interaction
 BSE| W_... = 1/ϵ v_...:     Direct interaction screened by 
 BSE|                        dielectric function ϵ(ω=0)
 BSE|
 BSE|
 BSE| The spin-dependent factor is for the requested Singlet is α = 2.0
 BSE|
 BSE| Excitation energies from solving the BSE within the TDA:
